<title>SPAIN: Spain's Banco Urquijo cuts prime rate to 6.0 pct.</title>
<headline>Spain's Banco Urquijo cuts prime rate to 6.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Banco Urquijo said it cut prime rate by 25 basis points to 6.0 percent.</p>
<p>It said it also cut mortgage rates.</p>
<p>The move follows the Bank of Spain's decision to reduce its key money market rate to six percent from 6.25 percent.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
